description:
Job title: SECURITY MANAGER
Location: Caracas, Venezuela
Job reference #: 33520
Contract type: International (expatriate) assignment. Fixed-term, residential contract. You will be required to relocate for this position.
Language requirements: Fluent in Spanish and English

At Eni, we are looking for a Security Manager to join Eni Venezuela. You will be responsible for planning, implementing, and overseeing security operations, ensuring the protection of personnel, assets, and business activities in compliance with corporate security policies and procedures. You will support the Security Division Manager in managing daily operations and ensuring alignment with business continuity and risk mitigation plans, while maintaining a strong understanding of the local context.

Your employment contract will be managed by Eni International Resources Ltd (EIRL).

Main responsibilities:

- Implement and monitor Eni programmes and procedures for the protection of Eni personnel, assets, accommodation, facilities and other interests;
- Implement Eni programmes and procedures for crisis management, emergency response and journey management;
- Review physical security measures and ensure that proper security systems are in place and functional in all existing facilities;
- Supervise manned and technical security contracts, ensuring compliance with Eni standards of service;
- Assist in emergency and contingency planning;
- Ensure security support in major meetings;
- Establish security information networks and provide “real-time” security advice to management and staff;
- Provide support to The Employer when analysing the risk of infiltration by organized crime;
- Provide security and crime prevention advice to company employees;
- Intervene promptly, together with The Employer, when a dangerous situation arises and threatens the safety of employees, contractors and third-parties as well as protecting the asset and Eni's reputation;
- Monitor the political environment for developments that could impact the safety of employees or the protection of assets;
- With reference to the monitoring of Security services and events, inform The Employer and the Central Security Functions on every event that is relevant to security that occurred within the area in question or in the pertinent productive units/organizational structures - including human rights violations - in accordance with procedures established in Eni's regulations;
- Co-ordinate protective support for personal protection;
- Develop security awareness among staff through training and management;
- Establish and maintain effective liaison with local Police, security forces, embassies and other relevant organisations;
- Develop a network of supplemental security resources, which support area security activities, if any;
- Liaise with Eni Central Security Function to ensure best practice standards are maintained;
- Provide assistance and monitor public relations and community engagement programmes as part of the wider security risk programme.

Skills and experience required:

- Previous experience in the oil and gas industry.
- Police/military background.
- Must possess negotiation skills and have demonstrated knowledge of diplomacy when dealing with multi-cultural issues for all stakeholders.
- Significant experience in security management.

How to apply:

- Applications are only accepted through our online application system.
- Please upload your CV in English.

About Eni

Eni is a global energy company operating in 61 Countries, with over 30,000 employees. Originally an oil & gas company, it has evolved into an integrated energy company, playing a key role in ensuring energy security and leading the energy transition. Eni's goal is to achieve carbon neutrality by 2050 through the decarbonization of its processes and of the products it sells to its customers. In line with this goal, Eni invests in the research and development of technologies that can accelerate the transition to increasingly sustainable energy. Renewable energy sources, bio-refining, carbon capture and storage are only some examples of Eni's areas of activity and research. In addition, the company is exploring game-changing technologies such as fusion energy – a technology based on the physical processes that power stars and that could generate safe, virtually limitless energy with zero emissions.

Eni International Resources Ltd

Eni International Resources (EIRL) is the specialist team that maintains Eni’s position as an industry leader for some of the best international talent in the oil and gas industry. By joining EIRL, you’ll belong to an organisation which truly values its people, and where you could develop a long-term international career by working on multiple Eni or joint venture projects across the globe.
When you join EIRL, we’ll assist with travel/relocation and visa arrangements, tax support and facilitating future reassignments. In addition, depending on your assignment contract, you may receive a comprehensive rewards package which includes a competitive salary, private medical insurance, pension scheme and, in some residential locations, housing, schooling and working partner support.

Working at Eni

At Eni we believe in enterprising people, capable of making a difference and making their contribution with passion and innovation, to respond to the global challenges of the energy transition. Learn more about global careers in Eni: watch our video testimonials or read more about what we offer our international assignees on our careers website. Eni will evaluate applications considering plurality and diversity as sources of enrichment. If your application is assessed to be among those most in line with the required profile, you will be contacted to continue the selection process.
Whatever your ambition, at Eni you can find the tools to make it happen.

Energy for action takers

#LI-EIRL
